# RotaHub Cursor Rules

## Code and Architecture
- Keep backend business logic in services, controllers should stay thin.
- Enforce DTO validation for every write endpoint.
- Maintain explicit job status transition validation.
- Keep SQL migrations in `supabase/migrations` as database source of truth.
- Keep Prisma schema synchronized with SQL migrations.

## Security
- Never log auth tokens, marketplace tokens, or service role keys.
- Store marketplace tokens encrypted (AES-256-GCM) before persisting.
- Do not expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in frontend bundles.
- Validate file upload size/type for POD endpoints.

## Data Integrity
- Preserve unique constraints, especially `job_assignments.job_id`.
- Keep `POST /jobs/:id/accept` atomic via transaction.
- Return HTTP 409 on assignment conflict.
- Require POD before DELIVERED when `POD_REQUIRED=true`.

## Documentation
- Update `docs/API.md` when adding/changing endpoints.
- Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for module/data model changes.
- Update `docs/SECURITY_LGPD.md` for security-impacting changes.
